//
// This is the SECOND Pact contract in the Queue vertical (epic #1232 Task
// 6): queue-bff (consumer) → queue-svc (provider), covering PostService.
// queue-svc now implements CreatePost, ListPosts, GetPost, UpdatePost, and
// DeletePost (Tasks 1–5 of the Post Composer slice — see
// services/queue-svc/src/queue_svc/handlers/post.py); this contract locks
// the wire shape those five queue-bff routes depend on
// (services/queue-bff/internal/handlers/post.go's PostHandler). The Post
// Composer **Scheduling** slice's Tasks 1–2 additionally land SchedulePost
// and RevertToDraft for real (Task 5 of that slice adds their two
// interactions here). The remaining PostService RPCs (PublishPost,
// BulkUpdatePosts, BulkDeletePosts, BulkImportPosts) still abort
// UNIMPLEMENTED in queue-svc, so no Pact interaction exists for them yet —
// they join this file as their handlers land (a later Bulk-ops story).
//
// The contract JSON at ../../../pacts/queue-bff-queue-svc-post.json is the
// authored source of truth (published to the broker by `make pact-publish
// SVC=queue-bff` and verified by queue-svc's provider-verification test —
// the Task 7 deliverable). These tests guard that the committed contract is
// present and well-formed and that it records the expected interactions +
// response shapes. Mirrors account_consumer_test.go exactly, substituting
// Account→Post.
//
// Every interaction here models the queue-bff→queue-svc gRPC hop
// (request.path is the raw gRPC method path, e.g.
// "/omnicore.queue.post.v1.PostService/CreatePost"; response.body is the
// unwrapped proto response, e.g. {"post": {...}} for CreatePostResponse) —
// NOT the browser→queue-bff REST envelope ({"data": ...}). The REST
// envelope is asserted separately by internal/handlers/post_test.go's
// happy-path tests. Post.status is modeled as the short lowercase string
// the queue-bff REST DTO uses (postJSON.Status via postStatusName, e.g.
// "draft") rather than the proto PostStatus enum's numeric ordinal or long
// name — an explicit, deliberate departure from how AccountGroup.group_type
// is modeled (a raw numeric enum ordinal) because Task 7's queue-svc
// provider verifier renders status through the same short-name mapping when
// satisfying this contract.
//
// Provider states (Task 7's queue-svc verifier must seed these EXACT
// strings — they are the consumer/provider interface contract):
//   - "an org exists" (CreatePost): org_id is sourced from the caller's
//     claims, never the request body (queue_svc.handlers.post.PostHandler.
//     CreatePost), and the RPC's own call is what inserts the post row — no
